## Real-Time Updates (Mercure)

This API supports real-time updates using [Mercure](https://mercure.rocks/), a protocol built on top of Server-Sent
Events (SSE).

### Mercure Hub Discovery

The Mercure hub URL and topic are automatically discovered via `Link` headers on supported GET endpoints.
Two headers are returned following [RFC 8288](https://tools.ietf.org/html/rfc8288):

```http
Link: <https://basil.local/.well-known/mercure>; rel="mercure"
Link: </users/{userId}/watch-files/{watchFileId}>; rel="topic"
```

**Supported endpoints for auto-discovery:**

| Endpoint                               | Topic                                                     |
|----------------------------------------|-----------------------------------------------------------|
| `GET /api/watch_files/{id}`            | `/users/{userId}/watch-files/{watchFileId}`               |
| `GET /api/conversations/{id}`          | `/users/{userId}/conversations/{conversationId}`          |
| `GET /api/conversations/{id}/messages` | `/users/{userId}/conversations/{conversationId}/messages` |

### Authentication

To subscribe to real-time updates, you need a JWT token obtained from `/api/security/real-time/token`. This token grants
read-only access to resources you are authorized to view.

### Topic Structure

Topics follow a user-scoped pattern for security:

| Resource | Topic Pattern |
|----------|---------------|
| WatchFile | `/users/{userId}/watch-files/{watchFileId}` |
| Conversation | `/users/{userId}/conversations/{conversationId}` |
| Conversation Messages | `/users/{userId}/conversations/{conversationId}/messages` |

### Subscribing to Updates

1. Obtain a Mercure token: `GET /api/security/real-time/token`
2. Fetch a resource to discover the hub URL and topic from `Link` headers
3. Connect to the Mercure hub with the token
4. Subscribe to topics using the EventSource API

**Example (JavaScript):**
```javascript
// 1. Get Mercure token
const token = await fetch('/api/security/real-time/token')
  .then(r => r.json())
  .then(d => d.token);

// 2. Fetch resource to discover topic from Link header
const response = await fetch(`/api/watch_files/${watchFileId}`);
const linkHeader = response.headers.get('Link');
const mercureMatch = linkHeader.match(/<([^>]+)>;\s*rel="mercure"/);
const mercure = mercureMatch ? mercureMatch[1] : null;
const topicMatch = linkHeader.match(/<([^>]+)>;\s*rel="topic"/);
const topic = topicMatch ? topicMatch[1] : null;

// 3. Subscribe to real-time updates
const url = new URL(mercure);
url.searchParams.append('topic', topic);

const eventSource = new EventSource(url, {
  headers: { 'Authorization': `Bearer ${token}` }
});

eventSource.onmessage = (event) => {
  const data = JSON.parse(event.data);
  console.log('Update received:', data);
};
```

### Update Events

Updates are published when resources change:
- **WatchFile**: Actors added, sources added, status changes
- **Conversation**: Metadata updates
- **Conversation Messages**: New messages, typing indicators

### Token Expiration

Tokens expire after {{ token_expiration_hours }} hour(s). Reconnect with a fresh token before expiration.
